			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-18T14:28:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				18,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mist): Rename library to Mist and update import paths\n\nUpdate the Mist library from lowercase \"mist\" to PascalCase \"Mist\" to align with project naming conventions. This involves three changes:\n\n1. **Cargo.toml**: Change lib name from \"mist\" to \"Mist\"\n2. **lib.rs**: Relocate clippy allow attribute from file header to module doc comment\n3. **integration.rs**: Update all module paths from Mist:: to direct module imports (Server, Zone, Resolver, ForwardSecurity)\n\nThis change ensures consistency with the PascalCase naming requirement throughout the CodeEditorLand project.",
			"SHA": "b681ca86e0b806c8b19e03125e7cc4a156db917d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-17T13:33:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				18,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Add Changelog documenting version history\n\nAdd new CHANGELOG.md following Keep a Changelog format to document all notable changes to Mist — the DNS sandbox element providing security-hardened local DNS resolution and per-extension domain allowlists.\n\nThe changelog tracks four releases:\n- v2.1 (Q2 2026): Documentation and formatting improvements\n- v2.0 (Q1 2026): DNS module maturation with 9 Rust modules and Air integration\n- v1.2 (Q3-Q4 2025): Foundation build with initial scaffolding and CI/CD\n- v1.1 (Q2 2025): Project inception as part of NLnet NGI0 Commons Fund\n\nThis provides a clear version history for contributors and users tracking Mist's development.",
			"SHA": "58cc381150501c248f2dbde1ead3e991c6da65b2"
		}
